From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oyvind Harboe <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Date: Thu, 18 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] DETAIL_PLACEMENT_ARGS reaches every detailed_placement call

detail_place.tcl passes DETAIL_PLACEMENT_ARGS to detailed_placement; the
four other calls -- after clock tree synthesis and after repair_timing in
cts.tcl, after repair_design and after repair_timing in global_route.tcl
-- are bare. A design that picks a legalizer for the place stage, say
`-use_diamond_legalizer -max_displacement {450 450}` because the default
negotiation legalizer could not place its wire buffers, is legalized by
the default again as soon as CTS inserts its clock buffers. Measured on a
1.5 M-instance hierarchical XiangShan: place legalized in 149 s with the
diamond search; CTS then ran the negotiation legalizer over 212,700
violations for 90+ iterations on the same floorplan.

Every call now takes the same arguments, and variables.yaml scopes the
variable to place, cts and grt so a build system passes it to all three.
docs/user/FlowVariables.md and variables.json are regenerated with
generate-variables-docs.py and yaml_to_json.py.

Not upstreamed; carried by bazel-orfs. Retires at a //:bump onto an ORFS
whose cts.tcl and global_route.tcl pass DETAIL_PLACEMENT_ARGS.
---
